  _menuDescription: May be seen chasing a road runner
  _funFacts:
  - _fact: Coyotes are the most vocal wild mammals in North America. Researchers
      have identified 11 different vocalizations they use to communicate, including
      growls, barks, yelps, and howls.
  - _fact: Coyotes are omnivores and eat almost anything available, including mice,
      rabbits, insects, and fruits. This varied diet provides free pest and disease
      control, especially by managing rodents that carry Lyme disease.
  - _fact: Coyotes have been known to form unique bonds with other species. They
      will sometimes hunt alongside badgers to catch ground squirrels, and have been
      known to travel through wildlife tunnels with them for safety.
  - _fact: Both male and female coyotes care for their pups, bringing food back to
      the den until the young ones are nearly 9 months old.
